IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Immigration (Guardianship of Children) Act 1946 (Cth) — THE NOUNS, THE RULES
-- AND THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C1946A00045.txt
-- (compilation No. 14, 14 October 2024). The child, or the adult who brings or
-- cares for them, asks: "Is this child a non-citizen child; is the Minister the
-- guardian, until when; can the child leave Australia; is what I do an
-- offence; by when must I seek reconsideration?"

§ `Nouns`

-- s 4AAA(2)-(3): with whom the child enters Australia.
DECLARE `Companion` IS ONE OF
    `a parent`
    `a relative aged 21 or over, other than a parent`
    `an intending adoptive parent`
    `another adult aged 21 or over`
    `no one`

-- s 6A(3), s 9: what I do.
DECLARE `My act` IS ONE OF
    `help the child leave Australia without the Minister's consent`
    `remove or entice the child from the custodian`
    `knowingly harbour or conceal the child from the custodian`
    `none of these`

DECLARE `Child case` HAS
    `the child entered Australia as a non-citizen`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child's date of birth`                                     IS A DATE
    `the day asked about`                                           IS A DATE
    `the child intends or is intended to become a permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the companion`                                                 IS A `Companion`
    -- s 4AAA(3)
    `an adoption class visa was in force on entry, and the adult will live with the child in a declared State or Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 4AAA(4), s 4AA
    `the Minister has directed that the child is the Minister's ward` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 6
    `the child has left Australia permanently`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 11
    `the Minister has exempted the child`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 6A, s 9
    `my act`                                                        IS A `My act`
    `I have a lawful excuse`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 11A
    `the decision came to my notice on`                             IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the Minister received my request on`                           IS A MAYBE DATE

DECLARE `Child position` HAS
    `the child is a non-citizen child under s 4AAA`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister is the child's guardian`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the guardianship ends at the latest on`                        IS A DATE
    `the child may leave only with the Minister's written consent`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `I commit an offence under ss 6A or 9`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the last day to ask for reconsideration`                       IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the last day for the Minister to reconsider`                   IS A MAYBE DATE

§ `Rules`

-- The 18th birthday; 29 February falls on 28 February in a common year.
GIVEN c IS A `Child case`
GIVETH A DATE
`the 18th birthday of` c MEANS `add months` (c's `the child's date of birth`) 216

GIVEN c IS A `Child case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the child is under 18` c IF
    c's `the day asked about` LESS THAN `the 18th birthday of` c

-- s 4AAA(1)-(3): under 18, entering as a non-citizen intending to settle,
-- not with a parent, a relative aged 21+ or an intending adoptive parent, and
-- not under the adoption-visa exception. (4): or a ward by direction.
@ref s 4AAA
GIVEN c IS A `Child case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the child is a non-citizen child` c IF
        `the child is under 18` c
    AND NOT (c's `the Minister has exempted the child`)
    AND (   c's `the Minister has directed that the child is the Minister's ward`
         OR (    c's `the child entered Australia as a non-citizen`
             AND c's `the child intends or is intended to become a permanent resident`
             AND NOT (c's `the companion` EQUALS `a parent`)
             AND NOT (c's `the companion` EQUALS `a relative aged 21 or over, other than a parent`)
             AND NOT (c's `the companion` EQUALS `an intending adoptive parent`)
             AND NOT (    c's `the companion` EQUALS `another adult aged 21 or over`
                      AND c's `an adoption class visa was in force on entry, and the adult will live with the child in a declared State or Territory`)))

-- s 6(1): the Minister is guardian until 18, permanent departure, or the Act
-- ceasing to apply (s 11).
@ref s 6
GIVEN c IS A `Child case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister is guardian` c IF
        `the child is a non-citizen child` c
    AND NOT (c's `the child has left Australia permanently`)

-- s 6A(1)-(3): consent to leave; helping a child leave without it is an
-- offence. s 9: removing, enticing, harbouring or concealing, without lawful
-- excuse. Each: 6 months or 2 penalty units.
@ref ss 6A, 9
GIVEN c IS A `Child case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I commit an offence` c IF
        `the child is a non-citizen child` c
    AND (   c's `my act` EQUALS `help the child leave Australia without the Minister's consent`
         OR (    NOT (c's `my act` EQUALS `none of these`)
             AND NOT (c's `I have a lawful excuse`)))

-- s 11A(3)(a)(i): "within the period of 28 days after" the decision comes to
-- notice: that day + 28. s 11A(4): "within 45 days after receipt": + 45.
@ref s 11A(3)-(4)
GIVEN c IS A `Child case`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last request day for` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the decision came to my notice on`
    WHEN JUST d THEN JUST (d PLUS 28)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN c IS A `Child case`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last reconsideration day for` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the Minister received my request on`
    WHEN JUST d THEN JUST (d PLUS 45)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@ref ss 4AAA, 4AA, 6, 6A, 9, 11, 11A
@export default The position of a child entering Australia to settle without a parent, and of the adults who bring or care for them, under the Immigration (Guardianship of Children) Act 1946 (Cth): whether the child is a non-citizen child (under 18, entering as a non-citizen to become a permanent resident, not with a parent, a relative aged 21 or over or an intending adoptive parent, nor under the adoption visa exception; or a ward by the Minister's direction: s 4AAA); whether the Minister is the child's guardian, and the latest day that ends (the 18th birthday: s 6); that the child may leave only with the Minister's written consent (s 6A); whether helping the child leave without it, or removing, enticing, harbouring or concealing the child, is an offence (ss 6A(3), 9: 6 months or 2 penalty units); and the last days to seek, and for the Minister to make, a reconsideration (28 and 45 days: s 11A). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Child case`  @desc The child's entry, age, intention and companion, any visa, direction, departure or exemption, my act, and the decision dates
GIVETH A `Child position`
`the child position for` c MEANS
    `Child position` OF `the child is a non-citizen child` c, `the Minister is guardian` c, `the 18th birthday of` c,
                        `the child is a non-citizen child` c, `I commit an offence` c,
                        `the last request day for` c, `the last reconsideration day for` c
